#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068488 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b89c50f3-2181-5b61-96cb-386ef88d2035" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Expression Involving a Power Function Multiplied by Its Derivative"}] :question/id #uuid "e2579380-1933-5819-a39e-9ffcfdafeeee" :question/math-academy-id "e-452" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int 6x^2(2x^3+3)^6\\,\\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "We note that $6x^2$ is the derivative of the quantity in the parentheses. So we make a substitution\n\n$$\nu=2x^3+3\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{du}{dx} &= 6x^{2}⟹du = 6x^{2}dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand rewriting our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int6x^{2}(2x^{3} + 3)^{6}dx &= \\int(2x^{3} + 3)^{6}6x^{2}dx \\\\\n&= \\intu^{6}du\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now solve the integral using the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\intu^{6}du &= \\frac{u^{7}}{7} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we substitute\n\n$$\nu=2x^3+3\n$$\n\nback in the expression. So the final result is\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int 6x^2(2x^3+3)^6\\,\\textrm{d}x =\\dfrac{(2x^3+3)^7}{7}+C\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068489 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fe2a279-0b92-561e-b17d-b902f43725ac" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Expression Involving a Power Function Multiplied by a Constant Multiple of Its Derivative"}] :question/id #uuid "9bf7d343-8d3d-5194-93c4-7b80bc1e3609" :question/math-academy-id "e-453" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int x\\left(1+2x^2\\right)^6\\,\\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "The $x$ that's outside the parentheses isn't quite the derivative of $(1+2x^2)$. The derivative of $(1+2x^2)$ is $4x$, so we're out by a constant factor of $4$. However, since we're out only by a constant factor, substitution will still work!\n\nSo we make the substitution\n\n$$\nu=1+2x^2\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{du}{dx} &= 4x⟹\\frac{1}{4}du = xdx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can now write our integral in terms of $u$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\intx(1 + 2x^{2})^{6}dx &= \\int(1 + 2x^{2})^{6} \\cdot xdx \\\\\n&= \\intu^{6} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}\\intu^{6}du\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve the integral in terms of $u$ and then write the final result in terms of $x$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{4}\\intu^{6}du &= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{u^{7}}{7} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{28}u^{7} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{28}(1 + 2x^{2})^{7} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068490 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18ce1807-3a09-5ebd-b3cd-a91db8d2b4a8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Using Natural Logarithms"}] :question/id #uuid "49f679c4-bbc4-59a5-9b0c-0f3b69d7cf57" :question/math-academy-id "e-454" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{x^2}{x^3+1}\\,\\textrm d x$." :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nu=x^3+1\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 3x^2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u= x^2 \\, \\textrm d x\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{x^{2}}{x^{3} + 1}dx &= \\int\\frac{1}{x^{3} + 1} \\cdot x^{2}dx \\\\\n&= \\int\\frac{1}{u} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\int\\frac{1}{u}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}u & + C \\\\ = \\frac{1}{3}\\ln & x^{3} + 1\\end{vmatrix}+ C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068552 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "03e934c8-da65-5615-9717-a50eee3577fd" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Other Fractional Expressions"}] :question/id #uuid "0461f8ba-c3c5-5e22-a679-32ee4f2a01b8" :question/math-academy-id "e-6149" :question/problem "$\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{x^2}{\\sqrt{1-x^3}} \\, \\textrm{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nu = 1 - x^3\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -3x^2 \\quad \\Longrightarrow\\quad -\\dfrac{1}{3} \\textrm d u= x^2 \\, \\textrm d x\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{x^{2}}{\\sqrt{1 - x^{3}}}dx &= \\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - x^{3}}} \\cdot x^{2}dx \\\\\n&= \\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}} \\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}\\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}(2\\sqrt{u}) + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{u} + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{1 - x^{3}} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264299 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b89c50f3-2181-5b61-96cb-386ef88d2035" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Expression Involving a Power Function Multiplied by Its Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd7c2fd9-ea0f-5a8f-9fb5-e122e38ff68f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(2{x}^{6}-3)^{3/2}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264301} {:answer/id #uuid "900cc2c2-bbf4-54e3-bfc2-2fc1d6cbbd2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2{x}^{6}-3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264302} {:answer/id #uuid "f767c3da-f088-5bc0-a73e-1f12c4c79085" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2{x}^{6}-3)^{3/2}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264303} {:answer/id #uuid "608cfc35-08e9-5f50-9fb8-84b52bb7b43b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(2{x}^{6}-3)^{3/2}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264304} {:answer/id #uuid "036c8bb9-5992-5e57-9db7-5ca37ccf0e06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2{x}^{6}-3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "608cfc35-08e9-5f50-9fb8-84b52bb7b43b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(2{x}^{6}-3)^{3/2}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264304} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7c19526-15af-5871-a26d-ee6b7ca831e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264300}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c6c7d03-b111-5ba6-842b-e6a7699ac04f" :question/math-academy-id "q-113581" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 12{x}^{5}\\sqrt{2{x}^{6}-3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We note that $12{x}^{5}$ is the derivative of the quantity in the square root. So we make a substitution\n\n$$\nu=2{x}^{6}-3.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =12{x}^{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=12{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand rewriting our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 12{x}^{5}\\sqrt{2{x}^{6}-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{2{x}^{6}-3}\\cdot 12{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now solve the integral using the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{{u}^{3/2}}{(\\frac{3}{2})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{u}^{3/2}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we substitute $u=2{x}^{6}-3$ back in the expression. So the final result is\n\n$$\n\\int 12{x}^{5}\\sqrt{2{x}^{6}-3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{2(2{x}^{6}-3)^{3/2}}{3}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264306 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18ce1807-3a09-5ebd-b3cd-a91db8d2b4a8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Using Natural Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f3e2f6c-1f81-5dae-918f-f20332f4fdce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{1+x-{x}^{4}}{1-4{x}^{3}}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264308} {:answer/id #uuid "77c4f64f-4dcf-5ecc-b7f2-5bdd694efc96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-4{x}^{3}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264309} {:answer/id #uuid "612f7c3b-f809-5e06-8606-8a6e2bbc1f85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+x-{x}^{4}|}{1-4{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264310} {:answer/id #uuid "931bf058-ea99-580f-b705-db9b79255f4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+x-{x}^{4}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264311} {:answer/id #uuid "401049fa-e789-5e01-abd6-3c330881b585" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{1-4{x}^{3}}{1+x-{x}^{4}}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "931bf058-ea99-580f-b705-db9b79255f4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+x-{x}^{4}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264311} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ccbc545-c5d9-5796-8468-508dea968569" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264307}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1aa2d253-0cbf-5398-8280-dd3f409dd30c" :question/math-academy-id "q-113719" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1-4{x}^{3}}{1+x-{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=1+x-{x}^{4}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1-4{x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=(1-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1-4{x}^{3}}{1+x-{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+x-{x}^{4}}\\cdot (1-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+x-{x}^{4}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18ce1807-3a09-5ebd-b3cd-a91db8d2b4a8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Using Natural Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a4a3527-1d72-5fdb-a089-532fdbe5f208" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{5{x}^{4}-1}{{x}^{5}-x}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264315} {:answer/id #uuid "ccdc77e5-27ce-593d-a63b-7e6fc23fdbc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{5}-x|}{5{x}^{4}-1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264316} {:answer/id #uuid "998d5f85-f282-553c-a200-6d8bfa5d6a03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{5}-x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264317} {:answer/id #uuid "b32f9438-22b3-5339-88b6-18cb9d83c5c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{{x}^{5}-x}{5{x}^{4}-1}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264318} {:answer/id #uuid "20135f12-15e9-586a-8225-14aa067ac4d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5{x}^{4}-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "998d5f85-f282-553c-a200-6d8bfa5d6a03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{5}-x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264317} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d9e84f5-60e7-5730-ab95-0ecb8d7392b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264314}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8791560b-d91e-5b13-8c37-2bc95b469824" :question/math-academy-id "q-113720" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{5{x}^{4}-1}{{x}^{5}-x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={x}^{5}-x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5{x}^{4}-1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=(5{x}^{4}-1)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5{x}^{4}-1}{{x}^{5}-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}-x}\\cdot (5{x}^{4}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{5}-x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "03e934c8-da65-5615-9717-a50eee3577fd" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Other Fractional Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cbef2a9-659d-5671-b00e-62fd423708bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{25(3-{x}^{5})^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264322} {:answer/id #uuid "575139dd-c0c9-5c70-bd5f-aed579eed5f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{25(3-{x}^{5})^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264323} {:answer/id #uuid "a0b907dc-88ae-5928-bcf9-373cc6431125" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{7(3-{x}^{5})^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264324} {:answer/id #uuid "a5389e1b-06ca-5b8a-b491-215f43c85082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5(3-{x}^{5})^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264325} {:answer/id #uuid "ac7a86d1-2d63-5252-9b51-3f44b1ebaf7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7(3-{x}^{5})^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cbef2a9-659d-5671-b00e-62fd423708bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{25(3-{x}^{5})^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264322} :answer-field/id #uuid "86956ba8-da3b-578f-816c-b3ee8789d18c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264321}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b444b962-ac59-54db-a1d5-c5787c4f1982" :question/math-academy-id "q-113726" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{7{x}^{4}}{{(3-{x}^{5})}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3-{x}^{5}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-5{x}^{4}\\,⟹\\,-\\frac{7}{5}\\text{d}u=7{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7{x}^{4}}{{(3-{x}^{5})}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{(3-{x}^{5})}^{6}}\\cdot 7{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{6}}\\cdot (-\\frac{7}{5})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{5}(-\\frac{1}{5{u}^{5}})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{25{u}^{5}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{25(3-{x}^{5})^{5}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fe2a279-0b92-561e-b17d-b902f43725ac" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Expression Involving a Power Function Multiplied by a Constant Multiple of Its Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bba25e9-ecce-5cf6-ba21-842081683042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{40}(x^{4} + 11)^{10} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065525} {:answer/id #uuid "eca1a03a-fc27-5da6-a150-e15fd02eb36f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(x^{4} + 11)^{9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065526} {:answer/id #uuid "0b0a7d0f-dcbf-5947-a080-fd1cf6aea5db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{44}(x^{4} + 11)^{10} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065527} {:answer/id #uuid "229c4b0b-a6bc-5362-a22b-74fa71ae5862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}(x^{4} + 11)^{10} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065528} {:answer/id #uuid "492128b8-b7ff-540c-846d-adbf8b42333e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}(x^{4} + 11)^{9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bba25e9-ecce-5cf6-ba21-842081683042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{40}(x^{4} + 11)^{10} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065525} :answer-field/id #uuid "4051453a-b829-5cc5-b870-9f05a94b3efd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065524}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "395d59bc-74f3-5209-b445-2d063af44516" :question/math-academy-id "q-12496" :question/problem "Calculate $\\intx^{3}(x^{4} + 11)^{9}dx$." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the ${x}^{3}$ that's outside the parentheses isn't quite the derivative of $({x}^{4}+11).$ But the derivative is $4{x}^{3},$ so we're only out by a constant factor. \n\nSo we make the substitution\n\n$$\nu={x}^{4}+11.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =4{x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u={x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can now write our integral in terms of $u,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{3}{({x}^{4}+11)}^{9}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{4}+11)^{9}\\cdot {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{9}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int {u}^{9}\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve the integral in terms of $u$ and then write the final result in terms of $x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}\\int {u}^{9}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{10}}{10}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}{u}^{10}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}({x}^{4}+11)^{10}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18ce1807-3a09-5ebd-b3cd-a91db8d2b4a8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Using Natural Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63167b53-3612-5995-b208-03463b8bf29d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{3}+10|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264329} {:answer/id #uuid "a44442e7-2fb7-5cd9-825b-d115742fc58c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{3}+10|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264330} {:answer/id #uuid "8ccc4d6a-3d3d-504f-8286-5e348d57768e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{3}+10|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264331} {:answer/id #uuid "95a1f104-5c7a-5e99-9483-61937af1eb88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{3}+10|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264332} {:answer/id #uuid "4361b0d4-3f7d-5f6a-a035-98670cd9c102" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{3}+10|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63167b53-3612-5995-b208-03463b8bf29d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{3}+10|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264329} :answer-field/id #uuid "022c7505-67ad-5203-9c69-27d163264700" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264328}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d1d9c00-0ef2-540f-a5d1-8f584b201b83" :question/math-academy-id "q-12501" :question/problem "Calculate the integral of $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{3}+10}$ with respect to $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={x}^{3}+10.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{3}+10}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+10}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{3}+10|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264334 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "03e934c8-da65-5615-9717-a50eee3577fd" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Other Fractional Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66cec056-a501-5f5d-a5b9-c636de5b0d92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18{({x}^{2}+5)}^{8}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264336} {:answer/id #uuid "63a2ab67-bdf0-57a9-aadf-e0154d71ca00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9{({x}^{2}+5)}^{9}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264337} {:answer/id #uuid "0b4cebb6-be18-520e-a22f-79e5e806d5fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2{({x}^{2}+5)}^{8}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264338} {:answer/id #uuid "b960bbe4-e2b6-53d2-ad7e-3f53cfebcebd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18{({x}^{2}+5)}^{9}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264339} {:answer/id #uuid "7ec85394-246d-5e4b-b15e-aea0de43c21e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9{({x}^{2}+5)}^{9}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b960bbe4-e2b6-53d2-ad7e-3f53cfebcebd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18{({x}^{2}+5)}^{9}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264339} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b982554-ba26-54ef-a5e7-41c7cf7543f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264335}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8fb950ae-e848-56f1-a15e-0130d381f980" :question/math-academy-id "q-12502" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{x}{{({x}^{2}+5)}^{10}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={x}^{2}+5.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{{({x}^{2}+5)}^{10}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{({x}^{2}+5)}^{10}}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{10}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{10}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{9{u}^{9}})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18{u}^{9}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18({x}^{2}+5)^{9}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069065 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b89c50f3-2181-5b61-96cb-386ef88d2035" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Expression Involving a Power Function Multiplied by Its Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4d53f9c-9ee8-593a-a46c-963b9421f842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x^{3} + 4)^{5})/(5) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066073} {:answer/id #uuid "14e5e253-8874-5726-a0a1-060fe4a3ba03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3x(x^{3} + 4)^{6})/(2) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066074} {:answer/id #uuid "41775c58-abc7-5f0e-a286-ac3ce5c216b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x^{3} + 4)^{6})/(6x) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066075} {:answer/id #uuid "45bcfd33-bca2-5172-8de7-a620e142f9a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3x^{2}(x^{3} + 4)^{6})/(2) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066076} {:answer/id #uuid "6f3954fd-89b1-5904-8422-efcff060dce0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x^{3} + 4)^{6})/(6) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f3954fd-89b1-5904-8422-efcff060dce0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x^{3} + 4)^{6})/(6) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066077} :answer-field/id #uuid "0489481e-0a83-5d01-91bf-d57dbce7e6d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066072}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "082a63d7-3326-5dca-8bbb-73a2f7476913" :question/math-academy-id "q-2189" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int3x^{2}(x^{3} + 4)^{5}dx$." :question/worked-solution "We note that $3{x}^{2}$ is the derivative of the quantity in the parentheses. So we make a substitution\n\n$$\nu={x}^{3}+4.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand rewriting our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{x}^{2}({x}^{3}+4)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{3}+4)^{5}\\,3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now solve the integral using the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\int {u}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{{u}^{6}}{6}+C\n$$\n\nLastly, we substitute $u={x}^{3}+4$ back in the expression. So the final result is\n\n$$\n\\int 3{x}^{2}({x}^{3}+4)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{({x}^{3}+4)^{6}}{6}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069066 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b89c50f3-2181-5b61-96cb-386ef88d2035" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Expression Involving a Power Function Multiplied by Its Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e737833-6a16-5255-9705-12d82cc3c809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x(x^{2} + 1)^{13})/(13) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066079} {:answer/id #uuid "28d71338-95c7-5e57-a222-276066aa72d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (2x(x^{2} + 1)^{12})/(12) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066080} {:answer/id #uuid "34d41f63-1530-586e-88bc-d63d42c6aeea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x^{2} + 1)^{13})/(13) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066081} {:answer/id #uuid "492e43c2-d010-59fe-9783-808db0b184f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x^{2} + 1)^{12})/(12) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066082} {:answer/id #uuid "63a79d8c-99f9-5689-b4f8-404fdd8c8802" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (2x(x^{2} + 1)^{13})/(13) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066083} {:answer/id #uuid "c381ea81-5ae6-5edd-ace4-037c3279c389" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x({x}^{2}+1)^{13}}{13}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264341} {:answer/id #uuid "44c787ab-fb5b-58e9-9fb5-b4635a4d9d69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x({x}^{2}+1)^{12}}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34d41f63-1530-586e-88bc-d63d42c6aeea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x^{2} + 1)^{13})/(13) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066081} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ba031b8-c494-513c-8d67-d2fa4f12632f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066078}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4b49482-74ae-5d27-81da-2160ac3cb246" :question/math-academy-id "q-2195" :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int2x(x^{2} + 1)^{12}dx$?" :question/worked-solution "We note that $2x$ is the derivative of the quantity in the parentheses. So we make a substitution\n\n$$\nu={x}^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand rewriting our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x({x}^{2}+1)^{12}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}+1)^{12}\\,2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{12}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now solve the integral using the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\int {u}^{12}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{{u}^{13}}{13}+C\n$$\n\nLastly, we substitute $u={x}^{2}+1$ back in the expression. So the final result is\n\n$$\n\\int 2x({x}^{2}+1)^{12}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)^{13}}{13}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fe2a279-0b92-561e-b17d-b902f43725ac" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Expression Involving a Power Function Multiplied by a Constant Multiple of Its Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d79b30d4-232d-5b8e-bcdd-799ff0c1d81e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{({x}^{2}-1)^{4}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264345} {:answer/id #uuid "634ba87f-6d30-5278-b812-f88773b06f90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{({x}^{2}-1)^{3}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264346} {:answer/id #uuid "a64c02db-4d8d-5cad-a4f4-2a18eef07f05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3({x}^{2}-1)^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264347} {:answer/id #uuid "20505da6-4432-5d9d-9939-3ad83f1ee3b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8({x}^{2}-1)^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264348} {:answer/id #uuid "ecf4e36c-9740-5ecd-8ec1-9682d015413b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{({x}^{2}-1)^{5}}{10}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d79b30d4-232d-5b8e-bcdd-799ff0c1d81e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{({x}^{2}-1)^{4}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264345} :answer-field/id #uuid "82696e52-c5fc-5dab-968f-522fc72627cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264344}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a45879ab-cfd1-5e43-9240-07874b933287" :question/math-academy-id "q-2388" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int x({x}^{2}-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the $x$ that's outside the parentheses isn't quite the derivative of $({x}^{2}-1).$ But the derivative is $2x,$ so we're only out by a constant factor.\nSo we make the substitution\n\n$$\nu={x}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can now write our integral in terms of $u,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x({x}^{2}-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}-1)^{3}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve the integral in terms of $u$ and then write the final result in terms of $x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\int {u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{4}}{4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{u}^{4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}({x}^{2}-1)^{4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}-1)^{4}}{8}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264350 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b89c50f3-2181-5b61-96cb-386ef88d2035" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Expression Involving a Power Function Multiplied by Its Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "280e0e5e-0e49-5ea2-b984-f7928b867fda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2(5{x}^{2}-4)^{3/2}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264352} {:answer/id #uuid "611be68e-9abf-5206-bcaa-377d8324a3f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(5{x}^{2}-4)^{3/2}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264353} {:answer/id #uuid "a4982a02-d6b6-59b0-9b6b-f3fcdc158918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3(5{x}^{2}-4)^{3/2}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264354} {:answer/id #uuid "207a978f-d4e6-5dfb-9c36-9b1120e969a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(5{x}^{2}-4)^{2/3}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264355} {:answer/id #uuid "eda11acd-0019-5a21-989b-8fdf3e45b037" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(5{x}^{2}-4)^{2/3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "611be68e-9abf-5206-bcaa-377d8324a3f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(5{x}^{2}-4)^{3/2}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264353} :answer-field/id #uuid "b873f10d-13ab-587a-ad58-0f88b18d76c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264351}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ba1168b-5db7-54a6-97ae-e4395967e964" :question/math-academy-id "q-2390" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 10x\\sqrt{5{x}^{2}-4}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We note that $10x$ is the derivative of the quantity in the square root. So we make a substitution\n\n$$\nu=5{x}^{2}-4.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =10x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=10x\\,\\text{d}x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand rewriting our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 10x\\sqrt{5{x}^{2}-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{5{x}^{2}-4}\\,10x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now solve the integral using the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{{u}^{3/2}}{(\\frac{3}{2})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{u}^{3/2}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we substitute $u=5{x}^{2}-4$ back in the expression. So the final result is\n\n$$\n\\int 10x\\sqrt{5{x}^{2}-4}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{2(5{x}^{2}-4)^{3/2}}{3}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264357 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18ce1807-3a09-5ebd-b3cd-a91db8d2b4a8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Using Natural Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad964a34-789e-5bdc-a9f3-9bc217bb0d5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264359} {:answer/id #uuid "88e927c4-db01-5e5f-9acb-3083979e40dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264360} {:answer/id #uuid "e6c38c72-32e5-579d-8df8-705113d97a2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264361} {:answer/id #uuid "3f04197b-41c8-5c9a-987b-c1b9d0a96eb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264362} {:answer/id #uuid "80a43864-2421-5603-adc5-6d9436b089b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f04197b-41c8-5c9a-987b-c1b9d0a96eb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264362} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ce48a20-c76b-5995-b281-686b4a293aa4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264358}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a679a08a-0056-5f32-a98b-af1f9cc68d04" :question/math-academy-id "q-49451" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{4x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={x}^{2}+1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "03e934c8-da65-5615-9717-a50eee3577fd" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Other Fractional Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b523a0b8-86e1-51da-9fa2-6970bc432d71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{{s}^{5}+1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264366} {:answer/id #uuid "1819c394-7905-5d47-99c9-7fc6ef63b133" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{{s}^{5}+1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264367} {:answer/id #uuid "750d4206-03ee-5401-a79f-a044a3b50dbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{{s}^{5}+1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264368} {:answer/id #uuid "71f35d7b-b832-5e72-93fb-ecbe6b49192e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{{s}^{4}+1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264369} {:answer/id #uuid "77188cee-e3b5-5f5b-b1c9-f54dc9cff659" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{s}^{4}+1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b523a0b8-86e1-51da-9fa2-6970bc432d71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{{s}^{5}+1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264366} :answer-field/id #uuid "73179b5d-3579-5b12-bbc5-2671bf6fd332" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264365}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "93ddd703-9a56-506d-ae6d-354420a2f0dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-49560" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{10{s}^{4}}{\\sqrt{{s}^{5}+1}}\\,\\text{d}s.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={s}^{5}+1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}s}=5{s}^{4}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u={s}^{4}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{10{s}^{4}}{\\sqrt{{s}^{5}+1}}\\,\\text{d}s & =10\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{s}^{5}+1}}\\cdot {s}^{4}\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =10\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\cdot (2\\sqrt{u})+C \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{{s}^{5}+1}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264371 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "03e934c8-da65-5615-9717-a50eee3577fd" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Other Fractional Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c78ff37c-aef3-5777-afa8-53dafa9a462e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{(1-{y}^{4})}^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264373} {:answer/id #uuid "a814a59c-e9fb-5a0f-a5cc-200cbb3e1bac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2{(1-{y}^{4})}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264374} {:answer/id #uuid "0b9bdd40-a299-52dd-8b07-46c2c564cb06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{(1-{y}^{4})}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264375} {:answer/id #uuid "a0496da4-d645-5a6e-a387-bbb9d3b36352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4{(1-{y}^{4})}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264376} {:answer/id #uuid "7c0888f0-cff3-5c5b-8b49-7986993b0f6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(1-{y}^{4})}^{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0496da4-d645-5a6e-a387-bbb9d3b36352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4{(1-{y}^{4})}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264376} :answer-field/id #uuid "1615c92b-d49b-5b8a-afc2-d6c55636a2cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264372}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86e72cd0-ebd6-5db7-8190-d10775b72433" :question/math-academy-id "q-49561" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{4{y}^{3}}{{(1-{y}^{4})}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=1-{y}^{4}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=-4{y}^{3}\\,⟹\\,(-\\frac{1}{4})\\text{d}u={y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{y}^{3}}{{(1-{y}^{4})}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4\\int \\frac{1}{{(1-{y}^{4})}^{5}}\\cdot {y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{5}}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{4})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-(-\\frac{1}{4{u}^{4}})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{u}^{4}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{(1-{y}^{4})}^{4}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264378 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "03e934c8-da65-5615-9717-a50eee3577fd" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Other Fractional Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7c4754a-e73d-5bdc-934d-001df9397581" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4{(9-{x}^{2})}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264380} {:answer/id #uuid "5a3ea406-137b-55da-9337-2297c2b43d85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{(9-{x}^{2})}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264381} {:answer/id #uuid "6d1cf99f-a35c-5642-89b7-fcf78168f94f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(9-{x}^{2})}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264382} {:answer/id #uuid "cfc53ce5-4d79-5d89-b712-2180ecc9c2c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8{(9-{x}^{2})}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264383} {:answer/id #uuid "1b69e3b9-c00e-5637-be03-0be0b7032f03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2{(9-{x}^{2})}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfc53ce5-4d79-5d89-b712-2180ecc9c2c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8{(9-{x}^{2})}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264383} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e05df33-8f27-5c9b-a7de-babf6203bb3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264379}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aed10256-1001-5ad2-b05d-1f5177778c2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-49575" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{x}{(9-{x}^{2})^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=9-{x}^{2}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2x\\,⟹\\,(-\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{{(9-{x}^{2})}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{(9-{x}^{2})}^{5}}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{5}}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{4{u}^{4}})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8{u}^{4}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8(9-{x}^{2})^{4}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264385 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b89c50f3-2181-5b61-96cb-386ef88d2035" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Expression Involving a Power Function Multiplied by Its Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6661a59f-94ed-52bf-887a-89a0a49d43ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{1+{x}^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264387} {:answer/id #uuid "68cf00ed-3464-5aeb-824b-7b913b822ffc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264388} {:answer/id #uuid "b09749f0-c48a-50a6-b88f-100179685cba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{(1+{x}^{5})^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264389} {:answer/id #uuid "abbf30c0-dcb1-5dff-ba80-afcb9ee6885e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{(1+{x}^{5})^{3}}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264390} {:answer/id #uuid "0a947d2a-ea68-59ca-834d-c63035e89758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{5}}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6661a59f-94ed-52bf-887a-89a0a49d43ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{1+{x}^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264387} :answer-field/id #uuid "cae0e4fa-dc80-5a73-a061-ea5fa25d8511" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264386}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "75e393fd-4391-50dc-8f83-4d49f1b94388" :question/math-academy-id "q-72382" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{5{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We note that $5{x}^{4}$ is the derivative of the quantity in the radical. So we make a substitution\n\n$$\nu=1+{x}^{5}.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =5{x}^{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=5{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand rewriting our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{5}}}\\,5{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{1/2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now solve the integral using the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{{u}^{1/2}}{(\\frac{1}{2})}+C \\\\  & =2{u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{u}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we substitute $u=1+{x}^{5}$ back in the expression. So the final result is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\sqrt{1+{x}^{5}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264392 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fe2a279-0b92-561e-b17d-b902f43725ac" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Expression Involving a Power Function Multiplied by a Constant Multiple of Its Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98c9e2ed-0185-57e8-b953-15603b82710f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}(2{x}^{3}+1)^{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264394} {:answer/id #uuid "b27c0095-576b-5eea-8907-358bade2fbfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}(2{x}^{3}+1)^{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264395} {:answer/id #uuid "d7fa3bc2-2c63-51c8-8c75-3a61f01749ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(2{x}^{3}+1)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264396} {:answer/id #uuid "887e047f-9bb3-5e3b-8bc1-0377bf0b0e2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}(2{x}^{3}+1)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264397} {:answer/id #uuid "0495a348-2b97-509f-8ea4-b03467d61f3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10(2{x}^{3}+1)^{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7fa3bc2-2c63-51c8-8c75-3a61f01749ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(2{x}^{3}+1)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264396} :answer-field/id #uuid "824b80fe-fbdf-515e-9ec6-62c647e8cb12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264393}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9eacc087-6f5d-506c-a5c1-601015ea4d5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72385" :question/problem "$\\int {x}^{2}{(2{x}^{3}+1)}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the ${x}^{2}$ that's outside the parentheses isn't quite the derivative of $(2{x}^{3}+1).$ But the derivative is $6{x}^{2},$ so we're only out by a constant factor. \n\nSo we make the substitution\n\n$$\nu=2{x}^{3}+1.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =6{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can now write our integral in terms of $u,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{(2{x}^{3}+1)}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{3}+1)^{5}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int {u}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve the integral in terms of $u$ and then write the final result in terms of $x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}\\int {u}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}{u}^{6}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}(2{x}^{3}+1)^{6}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264399 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fe2a279-0b92-561e-b17d-b902f43725ac" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Expression Involving a Power Function Multiplied by a Constant Multiple of Its Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b39419d9-ca01-5dce-bb20-0a0f40a67d95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{(1+{x}^{8})}^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264401} {:answer/id #uuid "0401dab2-8a86-5e52-b0c5-9c9ee8bbe390" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{32}{(1+{x}^{8})}^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264402} {:answer/id #uuid "5a65358a-86f6-5c00-aa93-69ec8a6f899e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{56}{(1+{x}^{8})}^{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264403} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ee78ce-e405-5882-a00b-1f8d5f8f97ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}{(1+{x}^{8})}^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264404} {:answer/id #uuid "508bed82-4382-59df-8e26-d422a62d6b86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{(1+{x}^{8})}^{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0401dab2-8a86-5e52-b0c5-9c9ee8bbe390" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{32}{(1+{x}^{8})}^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264402} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ff26cfe-7457-5934-9d06-b9cb9b3ec05d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264400}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9dab5184-0037-54fc-af6a-63bdd095c6d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-72386" :question/problem "$\\int 2{x}^{7}{(1+{x}^{8})}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the $2{x}^{7}$ that's outside the parentheses isn't quite the derivative of $(1+{x}^{8}).$ But the derivative is $8{x}^{7},$ so we're only out by a constant factor. \n\nSo we make the substitution\n\n$$\nu=1+{x}^{8}.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =8{x}^{7}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{8}\\text{d}u={x}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can now write our integral in terms of $u,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{7}{(1+{x}^{8})}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2{(1+{x}^{8})}^{7}\\cdot {x}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 2{u}^{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int {u}^{7}\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve the integral in terms of $u$ and then write the final result in terms of $x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}\\int {u}^{7}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{8}}{8}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}{u}^{8}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}{(1+{x}^{8})}^{8}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264406 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fe2a279-0b92-561e-b17d-b902f43725ac" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Expression Involving a Power Function Multiplied by a Constant Multiple of Its Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b110da93-620a-57a2-8c08-271e709122f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-5)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264408} {:answer/id #uuid "54ee440f-cd22-5ddc-a7c5-a1e576213592" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-5)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264409} {:answer/id #uuid "19cef8e9-cfdb-5d12-8dff-90a2cb74f658" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-5)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264410} {:answer/id #uuid "728a30c6-53ef-511a-9a23-6662da446741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-5)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264411} {:answer/id #uuid "8c9b925b-2874-5e8c-9e38-3cf3b4b156d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-5)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c9b925b-2874-5e8c-9e38-3cf3b4b156d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-5)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264412} :answer-field/id #uuid "a331e9b7-2dc3-5a72-81f3-9bf3ed251959" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264407}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf7f5f7a-6ce4-547a-a4d6-8bd8a66765fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-72467" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-5}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the $x$ that's outside the square root isn't quite the derivative of $({x}^{2}-5).$ But the derivative is $2x,$ so we're only out by a constant factor.\n\nSo we make the substitution\n\n$$\nu={x}^{2}-5.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can now write our integral in terms of $u,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-5}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve the integral in terms of $u$ and then write the final result in terms of $x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{3/2}}{(\\frac{3}{2})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-5)^{3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18ce1807-3a09-5ebd-b3cd-a91db8d2b4a8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Using Natural Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4289a01f-808b-5d1d-8045-6057025c8b58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-5{x}^{5}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264415} {:answer/id #uuid "601fc179-b89c-53ca-8b4e-2dfe057b5b56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2(2-5{x}^{5})^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264416} {:answer/id #uuid "d6337f79-2d71-5bdb-b7b1-ed33a6c2edf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-5{x}^{5}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264417} {:answer/id #uuid "d20ca3b3-b4e0-5387-9055-5f531c72cd4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-5{x}^{5}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264418} {:answer/id #uuid "24833536-e39b-5d08-8c88-291c9409b7f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5(2-5{x}^{5})^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6337f79-2d71-5bdb-b7b1-ed33a6c2edf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-5{x}^{5}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264417} :answer-field/id #uuid "704261b3-2289-5347-8d17-836f0a6ad08d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264414}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c16ee834-938b-51d7-9ce8-f471189eb001" :question/math-academy-id "q-72605" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{10{x}^{4}}{2-5{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2-5{x}^{5}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-25{x}^{4}\\,⟹\\,(-\\frac{1}{25})\\text{d}u={x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{10{x}^{4}}{2-5{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x & =10\\int \\frac{1}{2-5{x}^{5}}\\cdot {x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{25})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{25}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-5{x}^{5}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
